
---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "@/components/nav.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="IT & Cybersecurity Operations | Alfayo Robin">
  <Nav />

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pt-28 pb-12 text-[var(--white)]">
    <a
      href="/#projects"
      class="mb-8 inline-block text-sm text-[var(--sec)] transition hover:opacity-80"
    >
      ← Back to Projects
    </a>

    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--sec)]">
        Professional Experience • IT Infrastructure • Security Operations
      </p>

      <h1 class="mb-5 text-3xl font-bold md:text-5xl"> IT &
    Cybersecurity Operations
      </h1>

      <p class="max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 opacity-80 md:text-lg">
  My cybersecurity internship has provided practical exposure to security
  event monitoring, endpoint protection, patch management, and system
  administration in an organisational environment. Alongside this
  experience, I build my technical skills through hands-on cybersecurity
  labs and structured training, with a focus on developing toward a
  Security Operations Centre role.
</p>

      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">NetWitness SIEM</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">Bitdefender GravityZone</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">ManageEngine</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">Active Directory</span>
        <span class="rounded-full border border-white/20 px-3 py-1 text-sm">Microsoft 365</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">1. Overview</h2>
      <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
        During my cybersecurity internship, I gained exposure to tools and
        activities that support an organisation's IT security operations. My
        work and learning included reviewing security information in a SIEM,
        exploring endpoint protection, following patch management activities,
        and supporting system administration tasks. This experience helped me
        understand how security monitoring and routine IT maintenance
        contribute to protecting systems.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-semibold">2. Technical Experience</h2>
      <h3 class="mb-4 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--sec)]">
  • Cybersecurity Operations
</h3>

      <div class="space-y-5">
        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">NetWitness SIEM</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Gained exposure to SIEM monitoring by reviewing device information
            and security events in NetWitness. This helped me understand how
            security teams use centralised event data to support monitoring
            and investigation.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Focus: Security event monitoring and alert awareness.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Bitdefender GravityZone</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Used available access to explore the endpoint security console and
            learn how endpoint protection status and policy information are
            presented. My access was limited, so this is described as exposure
            rather than full administration of the platform.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Focus: Endpoint protection concepts and console familiarisation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">ManageEngine Patch Manager Plus</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Gained exposure to patch management activities, including reviewing
            update information. Patch management helps organisations reduce
            risk by keeping supported operating systems and applications
            updated.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Focus: Patch status awareness and routine maintenance.
          </p>
        </article>

        </div>

<h3 class="mb-4 mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--sec)]">
   • IT Support & Systems Administration
</h3>

<div class="space-y-5">

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">Active Directory and Microsoft 365</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Supported account-related tasks in Active Directory and worked
            with Microsoft 365, including SharePoint. These activities
            provided experience with user access and common organisational
            systems.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Focus: Account management, access support, and collaboration tools.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
          <h3 class="mb-2 text-lg font-semibold">IT Support and Maintenance</h3>
          <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
            Assisted with IT support activities involving user issues, IP
            phones, patching, backups, upgrades, and escalation where needed.
            These tasks reinforced the importance of system availability,
            reliable processes, and following established support procedures.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-70">
            Focus: Troubleshooting, maintenance, documentation, and escalation.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

<section class="mb-12">
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">
    3. Security Operations Workflow
  </h2>

  <p class="mb-5 leading-7 opacity-85">
    Security operations involve reviewing available security information,
    identifying items that may need attention, following established
    procedures, and escalating issues when necessary. My exposure to SIEM
    monitoring and endpoint security has helped me understand how these
    activities support an organisation's security processes.
  </p>

  <ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 opacity-85">
    <li>
      <strong>Monitor:</strong> Review available security events and endpoint
      information using the relevant tools.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Review:</strong> Identify events or status information that may
      require further investigation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Escalate:</strong> Follow established procedures and refer
      issues to the appropriate team or supervisor when needed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Maintain:</strong> Support routine patch management and system
      maintenance activities.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Document:</strong> Record relevant observations and work while
      respecting organisational confidentiality requirements.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="mt-4 text-sm opacity-70">
    This is a general security operations workflow informed by my learning
    and workplace exposure; it is not a claim that I independently performed
    every step.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mb-12">
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-2xl font-semibold">
    4. Evidence and Documentation
  </h2>

  <p class="mb-6 leading-7 opacity-85">
    This portfolio documents my technical learning and exposure to IT and
    cybersecurity operations. Evidence should demonstrate relevant skills
    while protecting organisational information and system confidentiality.
  </p>

  <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
      <p class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--sec)]">
        Workplace Exposure
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">
        Security Tools and IT Operations
      </h3>
      <p class="leading-7 opacity-80">
        My internship has provided exposure to NetWitness SIEM monitoring,
        Bitdefender GravityZone, ManageEngine Patch Manager Plus, and
        organisational IT support activities.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
      <p class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--sec)]">
        Hands-on Lab
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">
        Wazuh SIEM Home Lab
      </h3>
      <p class="leading-7 opacity-80">
        My independent lab uses Wazuh, Kali Linux, and Metasploitable 3
        to explore security monitoring and observe alerts generated
        during controlled exercises.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/projects/wazuh-siem-lab/"
        class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--sec)] transition hover:opacity-80"
      >
        View Wazuh Lab Write-up →
      </a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-12">
  <h2 class="mb-6 text-2xl font-semibold">5. Skills Developed</h2>

  <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Security Operations</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-7 opacity-85">
        <li>SIEM monitoring exposure using NetWitness.</li>
        <li>Familiarity with endpoint security using Bitdefender GravityZone.</li>
        <li>Understanding of security event review and escalation processes.</li>
        <li>Patch management exposure using ManageEngine Patch Manager Plus.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">IT Support & Systems Administration</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-7 opacity-85">
        <li>Active Directory account management and access support.</li>
        <li>Microsoft 365 and SharePoint support.</li>
        <li>IP phone configuration and deployment.</li>
        <li>Technical troubleshooting, maintenance, and issue escalation.</li>
        <li>Exposure to patching, backups, and system upgrades.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Hands-on Security Learning</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-7 opacity-85">
        <li>Wazuh SIEM home-lab setup and monitoring.</li>
        <li>Using Kali Linux for controlled security lab exercises.</li>
        <li>Observing Wazuh alerts triggered by Nmap and Hydra lab activity.</li>
        <li>Working with a Metasploitable 3 test machine in a virtual lab.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-5">
      <h3 class="mb-3 text-lg font-semibold">Professional Practice</h3>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-7 opacity-85">
        <li>Following established procedures and escalation paths.</li>
        <li>Documenting technical work and observations.</li>
        <li>Understanding access control and data confidentiality.</li>
        <li>Separating verified findings from assumptions during troubleshooting.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 p-6">
  <h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-semibold">6. Conclusion</h2>
  <p class="leading-7 opacity-85">
    My experience in IT support and cybersecurity has helped me understand
    how system maintenance, access management, endpoint protection, and
    security monitoring contribute to a secure and reliable IT environment.
    Through my internship and independent hands-on labs, I continue to
    develop the technical skills and practical understanding needed for
    <b> IT</b> roles,<b> Junior Cybersecurity Professional & Security Operations Centre (SOC) </b> roles.
  </p>
</section>

  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
